#: includes/class-ws-form-config.php:21234
msgid ""
"POSIX-style locale identifier from <code>get_locale()</code>: language and "
"optional region separated by an underscore, as WordPress uses for "
"translations (similar to POSIX / C locale naming; for example <code>en_US</"
"code>, <code>fr_FR</code>, or <code>es</code>). When a region is present it "
"follows ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 (uppercase). Respects multilingual plugins that "
"filter the WordPress locale."
msgstr ""
"POSIX-ähnlicher Locale-Bezeichner aus <code>get_locale()</code>: Sprache und "
"optionale Region, getrennt durch einen Unterstrich, wie WordPress es für "
"Übersetzungen verwendet (ähnlich der POSIX-/C-Locale-Benennung; z. B. "
"<code>en_US</code>, <code>fr_FR</code> oder <code>es</code>). Wenn eine "
"Region vorhanden ist, folgt sie ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 (Großbuchstaben). "
"Berücksichtigt mehrsprachige Plugins, die das WordPress-Locale filtern."

#: includes/class-ws-form-config.php:21240
msgid "Language Code (Site)"
msgstr "Sprachcode (Website)"

#: includes/class-ws-form-config.php:21242
msgid ""
"Primary language subtag from the site locale in ISO 639-1 format (e.g. "
"<code>en</code>, <code>fr</code>, or <code>pt</code>)."
msgstr ""
"Primärer Sprach-Subtag aus der Website-Locale im ISO 639-1-Format (z. B. "
"<code>en</code>, <code>fr</code> oder <code>pt</code>)."

#: includes/class-ws-form-config.php:21248
msgid "Country Code (Site)"
msgstr "Ländercode (Website)"

#: includes/class-ws-form-config.php:21250
